# Barcode Printing Implementation Plan (Trinity Pattern - Client-Side)

## Context & Requirements

The BCD library system needs three types of printable barcode documents:

### 1. Borrower Reference Sheets (A4)
**Purpose**: For LIBRARIAN use - reference guide to find the right barcode for the right student
**Layout**: All students grouped by class (new page per class)
**Content**: Student ID, barcode image, full name, "Élève" status
**Format**: A4 pages, browser printable

### 2. Student Library Cards
**Purpose**: Individual cards for students to carry and use for checkout
**Layout**: Individual card format with barcode
**Content**: Student barcode, ID, name, class, photo placeholder
**Format**: Card-sized (credit card or badge size), printable on card stock

### 3. Book Labels (Avery Stickers)
**Purpose**: Stickers to attach to physical books
**Layout**: 12 labels per page (3×4 grid)
**Content**: Barcode, item ID, library name
**Format**: Avery 5160-compatible (66mm × 25mm labels)

---

## Architecture: Client-Side Only (Vue Components)

**Key insight**: Generate everything in Vue.js frontend - no new backend needed!

**Why this is better**:
- ✅ **No new API endpoints** - Use existing `/borrowers` and `/catalog` endpoints
- ✅ **No new service layer** - All logic in Vue components
- ✅ **Simpler** - Just Vue components + print CSS + JS barcode library
- ✅ **Consistent** - Follows existing web UI pattern
- ✅ **Fast** - No server round-trip for HTML generation

**Approach**:
1. Create Vue components for each print layout
2. Use JavaScript barcode library (e.g., JsBarcode) to generate barcodes client-side
3. Fetch data from existing API endpoints
4. Use print CSS for layout
5. User clicks menu → Opens print page → Ctrl+P

