## Refined Implementation Plan (from Deep Analysis)

### Key Technical Decisions (from Step 2 analysis)

- **JsBarcode via CDN** (`jsbarcode@3.11.6`) - consistent with CDN-based architecture (no npm)
- **Barcode format**: Read from system settings (`barcode_type`: code39 or code128) via `/api/v1/admin/settings`
- **Layout**: Print routes hide sidebar via `route.meta.layout === 'print'` check in `App.js`
- **Item labels**: No `GET /catalog/items` list endpoint exists. Fetch all bibliographic records then items per record (N+1). Acceptable for small school libraries (~200-500 records). Batch with `Promise.all` for performance.
- **Borrower data**: List API enriches response with `class_name` and `barcode` fields - no extra API calls needed

